      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the smallest positive value of \\( x \\) such that \\( x + 5678 \\) results in a palindrome, we need to determine the smallest positive integer \\( x \\) that satisfies this condition. A palindrome is a number that reads the same forwards and backwards.\n\nFirst, let's denote the palindrome as \\( P \\). For \\( x + 5678 \\) to be a palindrome, we need:\n\\[ x + 5678 = P \\]\nwhere \\( P \\) is a palindrome. Since \\( 5678 \\) is a fixed number, we need to find the smallest \\( x \\) such that \\( x + 5678 \\) is a palindrome. We will start by checking the smallest possible palindromes greater than \\( 5678 \\).\n\nLet's check the palindromes one by one:\n\n1. \\( P = 1221 \\):\n   \\[ x + 5678 = 1221 \\]\n   \\[ x = 1221 - 5678 = -4457 \\]\n   This is not a positive value.\n\n2. \\( P = 2122 \\):\n   \\[ x + 5678 = 2122 \\]\n   \\[ x = 2122 - 5678 = -3556 \\]\n   This is not a positive value.\n\n3. \\( P = 3030 \\):\n   \\[ x + 5678 = 3030 \\]\n   \\[ x = 3030 - 5678 = -2648 \\]\n   This is not a positive value.\n\n4. \\( P = 4141 \\):\n   \\[ x + 5678 = 4141 \\]\n   \\[ x = 4141 - 5678 = -1537 \\]\n   This is not a positive value.\n\n5. \\( P = 5255 \\):\n   \\[ x + 5678 = 5255 \\]\n   \\[ x = 5255 - 5678 = -423 \\]\n   This is not a positive value.\n\n6. \\( P = 6363 \\):\n   \\[ x + 5678 = 6363 \\]\n   \\[ x = 6363 - 5678 = 685 \\]\n   This is a positive value.\n\nTherefore, the smallest positive value of \\( x \\) such that \\( x + 5678 \\) is a palindrome is \\( x = 685 \\).\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{685}\n\\]",
